---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | damienrobson">
  <article>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p>
      <strong>Last updated:</strong>{' '}
      <time datetime="2026-10-08">8 October 2026</time>
    </p>

    <p>
      Welcome to <strong>damienrobson.co.uk</strong>. This website is a personal
      blog operated by Damien Robson. I am committed to respecting your privacy
      and keeping data collection to an absolute minimum.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2 id="who-i-am">1. Who I Am</h2>
      <p>
        If you have any questions about this privacy policy or how data is
        handled on this site, you can contact me via:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>LinkedIn:</strong>{' '}
          <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/damien-r-4b9b37371/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            LinkedIn (new tab)
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        I use{' '}
        <a href="https://umami.is" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Umami Analytics (new tab)
        </a>{' '}
        to measure website traffic and understand aggregate reader interaction
        patterns on the blog.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>No Cookies:</strong> Umami does not set, store, or retrieve
          cookies or local storage items on your browser.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Anonymised Data:</strong> Umami does not collect personally
          identifiable information (PII). IP addresses are briefly processed in
          memory to derive general geographic locations (such as country) and
          are immediately discarded.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Cross-Site Tracking:</strong> Analytics data is strictly
          isolated to this domain and is never linked across other sites or
          shared with third parties.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>3. Web Hosting &amp; Server Logs (GitHub Pages)</h2>
      <p>
        This website is hosted on <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>, a service
        provided by GitHub, Inc. When you access damienrobson.co.uk, GitHub
        automatically processes standard technical access logs to serve site
        content securely and reliably.
      </p>
      <p>These server logs may collect technical data such as:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your IP address</li>
        <li>Browser type, version, and operating system</li>
        <li>Time and date of the request</li>
        <li>Referring page URL</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Purpose &amp; Legal Basis:</strong> This processing is conducted
        under our <em>legitimate interest</em> (and GitHub's operational
        requirements) to ensure network security, detect malicious traffic, and
        maintain server availability. For details on GitHub's data protection
        practices, please refer to the{' '}
        <a
          href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          GitHub Privacy Statement (new tab)
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Personal Data from Direct Contact</h2>
      <p>
        If you choose to contact me, I will use the personal details you provide
        (such as your name and email address) solely to respond to your inquiry.
        This information is never sold, shared, or used for marketing or
        newsletter lists without your explicit permission.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This website does <strong>not</strong> use advertising, marketing,
        tracking, or non-essential cookies. Because no non-essential cookies are
        set, you will not encounter a cookie consent banner on this site.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Your Rights (UK GDPR)</h2>
      <p>
        Under UK data protection law (UK GDPR / Data Protection Act 2018), you
        have rights regarding personal data, including the right to request
        access, rectification, or erasure of personal information.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because this blog does not use user accounts, tracking cookies, or
        individual analytics profiles, we retain minimal to no identifiable
        personal data regarding standard site visitors.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you have any concerns about how data is handled, you have the right
        to lodge a complaint with the UK Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)
        at{' '}
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          ico.org.uk (new tab)
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
